# Fixed 2026-11-24, defect 2754, lane-panel258-r1 (panel 258's R1): the
# shape beside the first case, a thread C ends that nobody waits for. Spec
# section 13: a thread nobody waits for aborts when `main` returns, saying
# how many, and so this program still does.
# Symptom: the abort said the thread was `still running`, of a thread C had
# ended 200 milliseconds before.
# Cause and fix: as the first case of defect 2754; the end of `main` tells a
# thread that ended without its answer as that (`runtime/parts/spawn.c`).
extern "fixedbugs-2754-thread-end.h"
    function te_nap(ms: i64)
    function te_end_after(ms: i64)

function worker(n: i64) -> i64
    te_end_after(ms: 0)
    return n

function main()
    t = spawn(worker, 7).must()
    te_nap(ms: 200)
    print("main returns without waiting for ", [t].len(), " thread")
